## 6. Upcoming programmes, events and opportunities

This needs its own management area. Not everything offered by the organization is a self-paced course.

Administrators should be able to create:

- Upcoming courses.
- Enrollment announcements.
- Live workshops.
- Webinars.
- Practical bootcamps.
- Training cohorts.
- Public events.
- Free introductory sessions.
- Special programmes.
- Application-based opportunities.

Each programme should have:

- Title and description.
- Cover image.
- Programme type.
- Date and time.
- Time zone.
- Location or online meeting information.
- Registration opening and closing dates.
- Capacity.
- Eligibility criteria.
- Price, if applicable.
- Application questions, if applicable.
- Visibility and publishing settings.
- Registration status.

Possible statuses:

- Draft.
- Upcoming.
- Registration open.
- Fully booked.
- In progress.
- Completed.
- Cancelled.

**Important:** An upcoming programme is not automatically an active course enrollment. Keep registration and course enrollment as separate records. A learner who registers for a free webinar should not automatically receive access to a paid course.

## 7. Learner management and access control

Founders need control over who can access what.

### Learner profile

Each learner profile should show:

- Full name and email.
- Account creation date.
- Preferred language.
- Enrolled courses.
- Payment history.
- Learning progress.
- Quiz results.
- Assignment submissions.
- Certificates.
- Account status.
- Recent activity.
- Support history.

### Access management

Superadmin should be able to:

- Grant access to a course.
- Revoke access.
- Extend access duration.
- Grant complimentary access.
- Enroll a learner manually.
- Move a learner into a cohort.
- Suspend or reactivate an account.
- Review access history.
- Set access expiration.
- See the reason access was granted or changed.

Every manual access change should record:

- Who made the change.
- Which learner was affected.
- Which course was affected.
- Previous and new access status.
- Date and time.
- Reason for the action.

### Staff roles and permissions

Do not give every administrator superadmin privileges.

| Role           | Responsibilities                                  |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
| Superadmin     | Full platform and business control                |
| Admin          | Manage assigned education operations              |
| Course manager | Create and manage assigned courses                |
| Instructor     | Manage assigned lessons, teaching and assessments |
| Reviewer       | Review and grade assigned submissions             |
| Support staff  | Handle learner support and account issues         |
| Learner        | Access enrolled learning content                  |

Permissions should be granular. For example, an instructor may be allowed to edit their assigned lessons but not change prices, issue refunds or grant themselves superadmin access.

