## 9. Payments and commercial management

The platform must support Rwanda's payment environment while remaining extensible.

Initial payment options to investigate and integrate:

- MTN Mobile Money.
- Airtel Money.
- Other supported payment providers.
- Manual payment verification as a controlled fallback.

Superadmin should see:

- Transaction reference.
- Learner.
- Course or programme.
- Amount and currency.
- Payment provider.
- Transaction status.
- Date.
- Verification details.
- Refund status.

Payment statuses:

(Verified) (Pending) (Failed) (Refunded)

Important rules:

- Never trust a screenshot as proof of payment.
- Verify transactions server-side with the payment provider.
- Protect payment credentials.
- Prevent duplicate payment callbacks from creating duplicate enrollments.
- Record refunds and adjustments.
- Grant paid course access only after verified payment or authorized manual approval.
- Never collect or store mobile money PINs.

The founder dashboard should distinguish money requested, money pending, money successfully received and money refunded.

