## 11. Founder intelligence and monitoring

This is different from a normal dashboard.

A founder needs to understand what is happening and identify problems before they become serious.

Recommended reporting areas:

| Report                | What to measure                              |
| --------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Learner growth        | Registrations and active learners over time  |
| Course performance    | Enrollments, starts and completions          |
| Learning performance  | Quiz scores and project results              |
| Revenue               | Verified sales, refunds and payment failures |
| Engagement            | Lesson activity and returning learners       |
| Programme performance | Registrations, attendance and completion     |
| Staff activity        | Administrative and teaching activity         |
| Support performance   | Open and resolved support requests           |

Add an activity and audit log that records sensitive actions.

Examples:

- Course published.
- Course price changed.
- Learner access granted.
- Learner access revoked.
- Payment manually verified.
- Refund processed.
- Staff role changed.
- Certificate revoked.
- Important system settings changed.

Superadmin should be able to filter these records by person, action, date and affected resource.

### Platform alerts

The system should highlight important operational conditions:

- Payment verification failures.
- Failed notification delivery.
- Courses with incomplete content.
- Upcoming enrollment deadlines.
- Assignments awaiting review.
- Unexpected spikes in errors.
- Expiring programme registrations.
- Suspicious administrative activity.

Avoid meaningless alerts. Every alert should have a reason and, where possible, a recommended action.

